after #286 2026-09-18 — #286 lane W: the 5b msgfile and its rendered sibling, committed as the wrap's own evidence

The push refused — correctly — on two untracked paths under notes/_lanes/286/W/: the 5b commit
msgfile and the .t3-rendered sibling the commit script writes beside it. Both are this wrap's
evidence (s218-D7 clause 3: evidence never lives in session scratch), so they are committed rather
than removed.

A lane that will not widen its own scope to clear its own blocker is the lane contract working —
and a wrap that commits its own leftovers instead of deleting them is the same discipline: the
msgfile is the only record of what was asked of the commit script.
